  "step_1": "The decision reason focuses on small probability outcomes (less than 20%) and applies a weighting adjustment: outcomes with probability below 20% receive a weight increased by 10 percentage points (i.e., their probability is boosted by 10 percentage points). It then computes a weighted sum of outcomes based on these adjusted probabilities and prefers the lottery with the higher weighted sum. In Lottery B, the 1% probability of winning 0 Euros is below 20%, so it would be subject to this adjustment. The adjusted probability for the 0 Euro outcome becomes 11% (1% + 10%). The other outcomes (2500 Euros at 33%, 2400 Euros at 66%) are above 20%, so they remain unchanged. In Lottery A, there are no outcomes below 20%, so no adjustment is applied. Thus, the decision reason can be applied to this problem and involves evaluating the adjusted probabilities in Lottery B and comparing the weighted sums.",
